12:07:19 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"\nYou are a memory patch editor for a materials computation agent.\n\nOutput contract:\n- Output ONLY Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks.\n- Do NOT output explanations.\n- Do NOT use markdown code fences.\n\nRequired edit format:\n<relative/path/to/file>\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n... exact existing text ...\n=======\n... replacement text ...\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n\nScope:\n- Allowed paths to modify: MEMORY/** only.\n- Never modify any other path.\n\nMemory rules:\n- Memory is a scientific interface, not an execution transcript.\n- Prefer reusable invariants:\n  1) System invariants (reference states, structure IDs, naming, units/definitions)\n  2) Method/protocol invariants (comparability-critical settings/definitions)\n  3) Result invariants (final reusable values with units/conditions/evidence path)\n- Do NOT copy raw logs/tool traces into MEMORY.\n- Do NOT add empty placeholder blocks (for constraints/questions/etc.).\n- Keep section schema stable so downstream parsers still work (e.g., Top Constraints / Active Open Questions headings).\n- Treat `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` as a latest-state snapshot; finalizer (`task_id == \"finalize_memory\"`) must write run-final state.\n- In `FACTS.md`, keep reusable scientific facts/method constraints/key conclusions with evidence; move path/layout tactics to `RUNBOOK.md`, and avoid pure path-layout Decision Log entries unless scientific interpretation changes.\n\nTopic schema contract:\n- `MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md`:\n  - Keep objective, definition of success, non-goals, and scope boundary.\n  - Do not put run-by-run logs or tool traces here.\n- `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`:\n  - For key results, include condition/method, units, and evidence path.\n- `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`:\n  - Keep reusable file/artifact index records.\n  - Prefer normalized records: `- PATH: <rel_path> | kind=<kind> | desc=<desc> | source=<task_id>`.\n- `MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md`:\n  - Keep hard constraints and soft preferences, with short source context when possible.\n- `MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md`:\n  - Keep unresolved blockers in Active and move resolved items to Resolved with closure evidence.\n- `MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md`:\n  - Keep stable reusable operating checklist and common recovery playbook.\n- `MEMORY/MEMORY.md`:\n  - Keep pointer-first index and concise state only.\n  - Do not duplicate detailed facts/path inventories from topic files.\n\nAdditional caution:\n- reports/latest_run/** is an audit snapshot and should not be treated as canonical memory source.\n- Text matching rules:\n  - Treat only text inside `<editable_file path=\"...\">...</editable_file>` as existing file content.\n  - If adding new content, anchor under an existing heading from the editable file text.\n- File-role routing:\n  - Keep `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` concise and pointer-first (current state + short summaries + pointers).\n  - Put reusable facts/decisions into `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`.\n  - Put artifact/path index entries into `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md` (prefer `- PATH:` records).\n  - Keep constraints/questions/runbook updates in their corresponding topic files.\n- Write-routing from task structured result:\n  - `facts` and `decisions` -> `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`\n  - `files` and `artifacts` -> `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`\n  - `constraints` -> `MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md`\n  - `open_questions` -> `MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md`\n  - goal/success-boundary changes -> `MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md`\n  - reusable procedure/checklist updates -> `MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md`\n- Minimality gate:\n  - Update only when content adds durable scientific value (system/method/result invariants, reusable decisions, stable constraints).\n  - Do NOT materialize every structured_result field by default.\n  - Skip low-value procedural chatter, repeated confirmations, or transient execution narration.\n  - `open_questions` should contain unresolved blockers only; drop speculative/self-referential questions.\n- Merge-first policy for `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`:\n  - Do NOT append blindly. Canonicalize and merge before writing.\n  - Treat `PATH` as the merge key (workspace-relative, normalized form).\n  - If a `PATH` entry already exists, update that record (kind/desc/source) instead of adding a duplicate line.\n  - Keep at most 1 canonical record per `PATH`.\n  - Keep `source` concise and deduplicated (prefer latest run/task context; avoid long source history).\n  - Exclude routine internal audit logs (`metadata/**`, `audit/**`, `.logs/**`) unless they are uniquely required evidence.\n  - Include scripts only when they are primary/reusable scripts referenced by summary/facts.\n  - Exclude intermediate scratch files and one-off patch helpers unless they are required for scientific reproducibility.\n  - Prefer scientific reusable artifacts over run-noise.\n- Conflict precedence:\n  - If `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` conflicts with `FACTS.md` or `FILES.md`, topic files are authoritative.\n  - Keep single-source updates; avoid duplicating the same fact/path across multiple files.\n- Quality checks before output:\n  - Ensure detailed facts and path inventories are not dumped into `MEMORY/MEMORY.md`.\n  - Ensure key claims include evidence path pointers.\n  - Ensure `FILES.md` path records follow the `- PATH:` style where applicable.\n  - Ensure `FILES.md` has no duplicate `PATH` records after merge.\n  - Ensure `QUESTIONS.md` reflects Active vs Resolved transitions when answers are available.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"\nRun id: run_20260227_040233_2ce157\nTask id: task_01\nTask goal (short): Generate an isolated O2 molecule in a large cubic box and prepare VASP relaxation inputs (gas preset) enforcing the triplet spin state.\nOutcome: success\n\nTask structured result (JSON):\n{\"summary\": \"Built neutral O2 from SMILES, generated boxed structure files under structures/o2, prepared VASP gas-phase relaxation inputs, and enforced triplet-spin INCAR settings. Verified required inputs at vasp_inputs/o2_relax/ with Gamma-only KPOINTS and ~20 Å cubic POSCAR lattice.\", \"facts\": [\"O2 was created from SMILES `O=O` as a neutral 2-atom molecule and written to `structures/o2/o2_box.vasp` and `structures/o2/o2_box.xyz`.\", \"A human-checkable XYZ copy required by task was provided at `structures/o2/o2.xyz`.\", \"Final VASP input set exists at `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/` with files `POSCAR`, `INCAR`, `KPOINTS`, and `POTCAR`.\", \"`vasp_inputs/o2_relax/INCAR` contains enforced triplet settings: `ISPIN = 2`, `NUPDOWN = 2`, `MAGMOM = 1 1` (total initial moment ~2 µB).\", \"`vasp_inputs/o2_relax/KPOINTS` is Gamma-only with mesh line `1 1 1`.\", \"`vasp_inputs/o2_relax/POSCAR` lattice vectors are cubic with side length 21.15093 Å (approximately 20 Å box target).\"], \"files\": [{\"path\": \"structures/o2/o2_box.vasp\", \"description\": \"Boxed O2 structure (POSCAR-style) generated from SMILES.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"structures/o2/o2.xyz\", \"description\": \"Human-checkable O2 XYZ file.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_inputs/o2_relax/POSCAR\", \"description\": \"Gas-phase VASP structure input for O2.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_inputs/o2_relax/INCAR\", \"description\": \"VASP relax INCAR with enforced triplet spin settings.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_inputs/o2_relax/KPOINTS\", \"description\": \"Gamma-only 1x1x1 KPOINTS.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}, {\"path\": \"vasp_inputs/o2_relax/POTCAR\", \"description\": \"POTCAR generated by preparation workflow.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}], \"constraints\": [], \"open_questions\": [], \"decisions\": [{\"decision\": \"Copied prepared files from `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/o2_box/` to `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/` to satisfy expected output paths exactly.\", \"rationale\": \"`vasp_relax_prepare` organizes outputs by structure stem; task expected root-level files.\"}, {\"decision\": \"Overrode/ensured INCAR spin lines with `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM=1 1`.\", \"rationale\": \"Triplet O2 spin-state enforcement is an explicit task invariant.\"}], \"next_steps\": [], \"artifacts\": []}\n\nEditable file snapshot (authoritative):\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/MEMORY.md\">\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: Execution plan committed (run_20260227_040233_2ce157, task `plan_commit`) with 5 work packages.\n- Latest run artifact: (none; planning-only task)\n- Next action: Generate isolated O2 structure in a sufficiently large cubic box, then prepare triplet-constrained VASP relaxation inputs.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Goal / principles: MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\">\n# GOAL\n\n## TL;DR\n- Primary objective: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Definition of success: Produce converged VASP outputs for isolated O2 (triplet) and report final energy/atom and O–O bond length with evidence.\n- Non-goals: Broader benchmarking or alternate chemistry systems outside isolated neutral O2.\n\n## Objectives\n- Generate isolated neutral O2 input structure in a sufficiently large periodic cell.\n- Run VASP geometry relaxation with appropriate spin treatment for triplet O2.\n- Post-process final outputs to extract total energy, energy per atom, and O–O bond distance.\n\n## Success Criteria\n- VASP run reaches acceptable convergence for the O2 relaxation workflow.\n- Final reported quantities include TOTEN-derived energy per atom (eV/atom) and relaxed O–O bond length (Å).\n- Results and key method settings are persisted in project memory with evidence references.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Exhaustive convergence/functional benchmarking unless required to achieve basic converged outputs.\n- Extension to other molecules, charged O2 states, or condensed-phase models.\n\n## Change log\n- [2026-02-27] Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\">\n# FACTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Canonical definitions: Isolated neutral O2 gas-phase workflow in a large cubic periodic box; report TOTEN-derived energy/atom and O–O bond length.\n- Verified facts: Execution plan is committed (5 work packages) for run_20260227_040233_2ce157 / plan_commit.\n- Tentative hypotheses: Planned default spin/box/input settings are defined but not yet executed.\n\n## Canonical Definitions\n- Target system: isolated neutral O2 molecule modeled in a cubic periodic simulation cell with large vacuum padding.\n- Primary reportables: final VASP TOTEN (eV), derived energy per atom (eV/atom), and relaxed O–O bond length (Å).\n- Spin intent: triplet O2 treatment via spin-polarized setup with constrained total magnetization.\n\n## Verified Facts\n- Plan committed for execution.  \n  - Evidence: task structured result for run `run_20260227_040233_2ce157`, task `plan_commit`.\n- Planned work package count: 5.  \n  - Evidence: same task structured result.\n- Planned execution sequence:\n  1) Generate isolated O2 structure in large cubic box.  \n  2) Prepare gas-phase VASP relaxation inputs with explicit triplet constraints.  \n  3) Execute relaxation and validate convergence.  \n  4) Optional static single-point on relaxed geometry.  \n  5) Post-process TOTEN, energy/atom, and O–O bond length and persist artifacts/memory.  \n  - Evidence: same task structured result.\n\n## Tentative\n- Default planning parameters (pending execution validation):\n  - Molecule/charge: O2 (neutral).\n  - Initial geometry source: generated from SMILES `O=O`.\n  - Spin controls: `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM={O:1}` per O atom.\n  - Cell setup: cubic box approximately 20 Å via `box_padding=10 Å`.\n  - Optional refinement: static single-point after relaxation.\n\n## Decision Log\n- [2026-02-27 | run_20260227_040233_2ce157 / plan_commit] Plan committed. Rationale: approved for execution.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\">\n# FILES\n\n## TL;DR\n- Entry points: (empty)\n- Primary artifacts: (empty)\n\n## Index\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\">\n# CONSTRAINTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Hard constraints:\n  - (empty)\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- (empty)\n\n## Soft Preferences\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\">\n# QUESTIONS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Active blockers: (empty)\n\n## Active\n- (empty)\n\n## Resolved\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\">\n# RUNBOOK\n\n## TL;DR\n- Standard operating procedure pointer file.\n- For this project class (isolated-molecule VASP), use a plan-first then execute/post-process sequence.\n\n## Checklist\n1. Confirm goal and success criteria from task packet.\n2. Read MEMORY.md first, then locate details via rg/sed.\n3. Persist large outputs to files and cite paths.\n4. Finish using the active task runner contract (control tool finish/fail or structured response).\n5. For isolated O2 runs, build structure in a sufficiently large cubic box before input generation.\n6. Apply explicit triplet spin settings during relaxation input preparation.\n7. Validate electronic/ionic convergence after relaxation before extracting metrics.\n8. Optionally run a static single-point on relaxed geometry for cleaner final energy reporting.\n9. Post-process and record: TOTEN, energy/atom (eV/atom), and O–O bond length (Å), with evidence paths.\n\n</editable_file>\n","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"high","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
