12:08:29 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.2:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"You are the Director of the Standard lane (dynamic execution controller).\n\nYou may use helper tools for read/check inspection before deciding.\nYou MUST finish with exactly one `director_decide` control call in its own turn.\nHelper tool available in this stage:\n- `bash_exec`\n\nInputs you will receive (in context message):\n- User request\n- Current proposal (markdown) + work_packages order\n- Memory index (autoload excerpt)\n- AlreadyDone: summaries of completed tasks\n- Available tools for task runner\n\nAllowed states:\n- PerformNextTask: emit one concrete `task_packet` for task runner.\n  - task_packet fields: goal, task_detail, expected_outputs, suggested_tools, reference_hint.\n  - task_detail must contain only: goal, key invariants, and done criteria; keep it within 3 short paragraphs/bullet blocks.\n  - Do not copy long text from proposal/memory.\n  - expected_outputs default shape:\n    - primary artifact path(s)\n    - 1-3 key numeric results with units\n    - brief validation verdict (PASS/FAIL + evidence path)\n  - Tool schemas are authoritative. Do not include full parameter templates in task_detail; include only required overrides/invariants.\n- MinorReviseProposal: small/local edits that keep the same route.\n- MajorReviseProposal: route-level change is required.\n- StopAndSynthesize: execution is complete or user asked planning-only output.\n\nDecision semantics:\n- Default priority: PerformNextTask > MinorReviseProposal > MajorReviseProposal.\n- Do not choose MajorReviseProposal when safe defaults/local edits can keep route valid.\n- If worker reports remote job failures, default to MajorReviseProposal and rerun only failed subset.\n- Do not treat proposal-format requirements as Director completion criteria.\n\nRules:\n- Avoid repeating completed work; consult AlreadyDone + memory index.\n- Never ask the worker to read metadata/internal run paths.\n- Never ask the worker to edit `MEMORY/**` or call `memory_apply_aider_edits`.\n- Preserve key parameters from proposal/default tables; do NOT weaken to conditional wording.\n- For PerformNextTask, task_packet.suggested_tools are advisory only and must be selected from available tools.\n- One decision finalization per turn: call `director_decide` exactly once, alone.\n- Assume runtime environment is correctly configured per project README; do not escalate runtime/tooling prerequisites as human-blocking by default.\n- Do not revise or ask for confirmation for minor execution details; apply safe defaults and continue.\n- Keep `director_decide.rationale` very short (usually 1-2 sentences).\n- If proposal has unresolved BLOCKING items, use MajorReviseProposal with updated proposal/work packages and concise HITL questions.\n\nWhen ready, you MUST call `director_decide`.\n\n\nTermination contract:\n- End with exactly one `director_decide` control tool call in its own turn.\n- Do not output plain final text as the terminal response.","role":"system"},{"content":"User request:\nCompute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n\nProposal:\n# Items needing human decision\n- (none)\n\n# Key parameters (defaults)\n\n| Parameter | Default | Confidence | Rationale |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| Molecule / charge | O2 (neutral) | High | Target system: isolated O2 molecule. |\n| Initial geometry | Generated from SMILES `O=O` (triplet-friendly start) | Medium | RDKit geometry is a reasonable starting point; VASP relaxation will refine. |\n| Spin state | Triplet via `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM={O:1}` (per atom) | Medium | Ground state of O2 is triplet; NUPDOWN enforces correct total magnetization. |\n| Box size | Cubic, ~20 Å (via `box_padding=10 Å`) | High | Minimizes intermolecular interactions under PBC for a diatomic. |\n| KPOINTS | 1×1×1 (Gamma) | High | Gas-phase molecule in a large box. |\n| Exchange–correlation / POTCAR | MPRelaxSet defaults (PBE, PBE54 potentials if configured) | Medium | Standard, reproducible baseline matching provided prep tools. |\n| ENCUT | 520 eV | High | MPRelaxSet default; typically sufficient for O. |\n| Relaxation | Ionic relaxation only (`ISIF=2`, `IBRION=2`, `EDIFFG≈-0.02 eV/Å`, `NSW≈500`) | High | Optimize bond length while keeping box fixed. |\n| Symmetry | `ISYM=0` | High | Gas preset generally disables symmetry to avoid issues for molecules. |\n| Final energy definition | Use final electronic total energy (TOTEN) from relaxation **or** from a follow-up static single-point on relaxed geometry | Medium | Static SP is often cleaner for reporting; relaxation final energy is acceptable if converged. |\n| Reported metrics | (1) Energy per atom = TOTEN/2 (eV/atom); (2) O–O distance from final CONTCAR/CONTCAR-equivalent (Å) | High | Exactly what user requested. |\n\n# Execution plan\n\n## 1) Create O2-in-a-box structure\n- Use `create_molecule_from_smiles` with SMILES `O=O`.\n- Write both an XYZ (for inspection) and a VASP/POSCAR-style structure with a cubic box.\n- Default: `box_padding=10` Å (≈20 Å lattice).\n- Store under a clear workspace path, e.g. `structures/o2/o2_box.vasp` (and `structures/o2/o2.xyz`).\n\n## 2) Prepare VASP relaxation inputs from scratch\n- Use `vasp_relax_prepare` targeting the generated POSCAR/VASP structure.\n- Set `calc_type='gas'` to force 1×1×1 k-mesh, `ISYM=0`, and molecule-friendly defaults.\n- Provide `user_incar_settings` to enforce the correct spin:\n  - `NUPDOWN=2`\n  - `MAGMOM={\"O\": 1}` (or {\"O\":2} depending on tool conventions; verify after generation)\n  - Optionally tighten convergence if needed (e.g. `EDIFF=1e-7`, `EDIFFG=-0.01`) after the first attempt.\n- Output to a dedicated input directory (e.g. `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/…`).\n\n## 3) Run VASP\n- Use `vasp_execute_batch` in single-folder mode on the created relax folder.\n- Write outputs to an external output root (e.g. `vasp_runs/o2_relax/…`) to keep clean separation between inputs and outputs.\n- Verify success criteria from VASP outputs:\n  - Electronic convergence reached (OSZICAR/OUTCAR)\n  - Ionic convergence reached (forces below threshold; check final `F=` lines / `TOTAL-FORCE` section)\n\n## 4) (Recommended) Single-point energy on relaxed geometry\n- If relaxation completed, run a static calculation for a clean final energy:\n  - Use `vasp_sp_prepare` with `calc_type='gas'` on the relaxed structure (CONTCAR).\n  - Override with `NSW=0`, `IBRION=-1` (and keep spin settings `NUPDOWN=2`, `ISPIN=2`).\n  - Execute with `vasp_execute_batch`.\n- Use the static run’s final TOTEN for reporting; use the relaxed geometry (bond length) from the relaxation CONTCAR.\n\n## 5) Post-process and report: energy/atom and bond distance\n- Use a small analysis script (via `bash_exec` + Python) to:\n  - Read final energy (TOTEN) from OUTCAR (fallback: OSZICAR) of the chosen run (static preferred).\n  - Compute energy per atom: `E_atom = TOTEN / 2`.\n  - Read final positions from CONTCAR and compute O–O bond length (minimum-image distance to be safe).\n- Persist results to a short text/JSON artifact (e.g. `results/o2_summary.json`) containing:\n  - run paths used\n  - TOTEN (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom)\n  - bond length (Å)\n  - key INCAR settings snapshot (ISPIN/NUPDOWN/ENCUT)\n\n## 6) Recordkeeping\n- Write the final numbers and file pointers into `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md` and `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md` using `memory_apply_aider_edits` (in execution stage), so the project has a canonical record.\n\n# Deliverables\n- VASP input set(s) for O2 relax (and optional static SP).\n- Completed VASP output directory with OUTCAR/OSZICAR/CONTCAR.\n- Reported:\n  - Final energy per atom (eV/atom)\n  - Final O–O bond distance (Å)\n  - Paths to the exact files used to extract these results.\n\n\nWork packages (ordered advisory milestones, not a fixed task script):\n[\"Generate isolated O2 structure in a sufficiently large cubic box\", \"Prepare VASP relaxation inputs (gas preset) with explicit triplet spin constraints\", \"Execute VASP relaxation and validate convergence\", \"(Optional but recommended) Prepare and run a static single-point on the relaxed geometry\", \"Post-process VASP outputs to extract TOTEN, compute energy/atom, and compute O–O bond length; persist result artifacts and update project memory\"]\n\nMemory index (autoload excerpt):\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Execute VASP relaxation for isolated triplet O2 and report final energy per atom and relaxed O–O bond distance.\n- Current milestone: `task_01` (run_20260227_040233_2ce157) completed O2 structure generation and VASP relaxation input preparation.\n- Latest run artifact: `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/{POSCAR,INCAR,KPOINTS,POTCAR}` plus structure files under `structures/o2/`.\n- Next action: Run VASP relaxation from `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/`, verify convergence, then post-process TOTEN-derived metrics.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Preserve triplet-spin setup for O2 relaxation (`ISPIN = 2`, `NUPDOWN = 2`, `MAGMOM = 1 1`).\n2. Keep isolated gas-phase setup comparable (large cubic box; Gamma-only `1 1 1` k-point sampling).\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Goal / principles: MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\nAlreadyDone (sanitized summary; metadata/internal paths omitted):\n[{\"task_id\": \"task_01\", \"outcome\": \"success\", \"summary\": \"Built neutral O2 from SMILES, generated boxed structure files under structures/o2, prepared VASP gas-phase relaxation inputs, and enforced triplet-spin INCAR settings. Verified required inputs at vasp_inputs/o2_relax/ with Gamma-only KPOINTS and ~20 Å cubic POSCAR lattice.\", \"decisions\": [\"Copied prepared files from `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/o2_box/` to `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/` to satisfy expected output paths... (`vasp_relax_prepare` organizes outputs by structure stem; task expected root-level files.)\", \"Overrode/ensured INCAR spin lines with `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM=1 1`. (Triplet O2 spin-state enforcement is an explicit task invariant.)\"], \"facts\": [\"O2 was created from SMILES `O=O` as a neutral 2-atom molecule and written to `structures/o2/o2_box.vasp` and `structures/o2/o2_box.xyz`.\", \"A human-checkable XYZ copy required by task was provided at `structures/o2/o2.xyz`.\", \"Final VASP input set exists at `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/` with files `POSCAR`, `INCAR`, `KPOINTS`, and `POTCAR`.\"]}]\n\nTask status board (structured task history with outcomes):\n[{\"task_id\": \"task_01\", \"status\": \"success\", \"goal\": \"Generate an isolated O2 molecule in a large cubic box and prepare VASP relaxation inputs (gas preset) enforcing the triplet spin state.\", \"outcome\": \"success\", \"summary\": \"Built neutral O2 from SMILES, generated boxed structure files under structures/o2, prepared VASP gas-phase relaxation inputs, and enforced triplet-spin INCAR settings. Verified required inputs at vasp_inputs/o2_relax/...\", \"decision_count\": 2}]\n\nAvailable tools for task runner:\ncreate_molecule_from_smiles : \n    Build a 3D molecule from a SMILES string using RDKit. Specially, pay attention to the formal charge of the SMILES string, RDkit will check the charge and add Hs to the molecule to make it neutral.\n    \n\nmace_relax_batch : Submit multiple MACE relaxations in one DPDispatcher submission. Preferred tool for batch MACE relaxations.\n\nmace_sp_batch : Run MACE single-point jobs for structures under one directory.\n\nvasp_relax_prepare : \n    Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP relax inputs with calc_type presets and k_product k-mesh.\n    Also can be modified for other calculation types by overriding INCAR via the user_incar_settings.\n    Support exts: .vasp, .cif\n\n    Baseline DFT settings follow Materials Project MPRelaxSet (key defaults):\n    - PBE54 POTCARS, ENCUT=520 eV, PREC=Accurate, ISPIN=2, IBRION=2, LREAL=AUTO, LASPH=True, LWAVE=False, LCHARG=False.\n    - Additional overrides applied based on calc_type: ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.1 for bulk/slab; ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.01 for gas.\n    - ISIF policy: bulk with relax_cell=False -> ISIF=2; bulk with relax_cell=True -> ISIF=3.\n      slab and gas always use ISIF=2, where slab forces KPOINTS z=1 and gas forces KPOINTS 1x1x1 with ISYM=0, LREAL=False.\n    - Improved convergence settings: EDIFF=1e-6; NSW=500; EDIFFG=-0.02;\n    - LORBIT is controlled by compute_dos (default False -> LORBIT=0, True -> LORBIT=11).\n    - KPOINTS is generated by k*a=k_product, where a is the lattice constant in Angstrom. Set to 30 by default and sufficient for most systems.\n    - DFT-D3 and DFT+U are disabled by default. Enable them if the system is adsorption system(DFT-D3) or transition metal oxide system(DFT+U).\n    \n\nvasp_sp_prepare : Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP single-point inputs for structures under a file or directory.\n\nbuild_slab : Build slabs for all terminations of a Miller index from bulk structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of bulk_structure or bulk_dir. When bulk_dir is used, output_root is required.\n    Batch outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path\n    (without suffix) using '__'.\n    \n\nfix_atoms_by_layers : Fix (freeze) the bottom N atomic layers of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_layers.json.\n    \n\nfix_atoms_by_height : Fix (freeze) atoms within specified z ranges of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_height.json.\n    \n\nsupercell : Create supercells from structure file(s). THIS WILL LOSE ALL SELECTIVE DYNAMICS INFORMATION.\n    Provide exactly one of structure_file or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<structure_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_supercell.json.\n\n    The JSON format is:\n    {\n      \"results\": [\n        {\"input_rel\": \"a/CO.vasp\", \"structure_id\": \"a__CO\", \"output_rel\": \"out/a__CO.vasp\", \"natoms\": 2}\n      ]\n    }\n\n    \n\nenumerate_adsorption_sites : \n    Enumerate adsorption sites on a slab using ASF. Use it only for small scale placement.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_json:\n    [\n      {\"label\": \"ontop_0\", \"kind\": \"ontop\", \"cart_coords\": [x, y, z]}\n    ]\n    The returned tool data includes the workspace-relative path in \"sites\" and \"sites_json_rel\".\n    \n\nplace_adsorbate : Place an adsorbate molecule on a slab. Use it only if for small scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    It writes metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json and an ads_indices index JSON.\n\ngenerate_batch_adsorption_structures : \n    Generate multiple adsorbed structures up to max_structures. Suitable for large scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    Input can be a single slab file (slab_file) or a directory of slab files (slab_dir).\n    When slab_dir is used, each slab gets its own subdirectory under output_dir. Max_structures applies per slab.\n    For nested slab_dir layouts, slab_id encodes the relative path (without suffix) using '__'.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_dir/batch_structures.json and a per-structure\n    metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json with ads_indices.\n    It also writes output_dir/ads_indices.json as an index file:\n    [\n      {\n        \"slab_file_rel\": \"slabs/fe111.vasp\",\n        \"slab_id\": \"fe111\",\n        \"label\": \"ontop_0\",\n        \"output_poscar_rel\": \"adsorption/batch/fe111/ontop_0.vasp\",\n        \"ads_indices_added\": [36],\n        \"ads_indices\": [36]\n      }\n    ]\n    The returned tool data replaces \"structures\" with the workspace-relative path to this JSON file.\n    \n\nmake_neb_geometry : \n    Generate NEB interpolation geometries in nebmake.pl style.\n\n    The tool validates that initial and final structures have the same element order, atom count,\n    and lattice (within tolerance). Images are written under output_dir/00..(NI+1) with output_filename.\n    Selective dynamics constraints are preserved if present in the input files (ASE handles constraints).\n    \n\nmake_neb_incar : \n    Generate a VTST NEB/CI-NEB INCAR based on a template INCAR.\n\n    The tool parses the template INCAR (ignores comments/blank lines, case-insensitive keys),\n    applies NEB overrides, and writes the final INCAR along with a patch JSON.\n    \n\nvasp_execute_batch : Submit VASP runs in one DPDispatcher submission (single-folder or recursive batch modes).\n\nmp_search_materials : \n    Search Materials Project with flexible criteria and write results to CSV.\n\n    Common criteria keys (pass via `criteria`):\n      - material_ids (list[str] or str)\n      - elements (list[str] or str)\n      - chemsys (str)\n      - formula (str)\n      - is_stable (bool)\n      - energy_above_hull ([min, max])\n      - formation_energy ([min, max])\n      - band_gap ([min, max])\n      - crystal_system (str)\n      - spacegroup_number / spacegroup_symbol\n      - num_sites ([min, max])\n      - density ([min, max])\n      - volume ([min, max])\n      - num_elements ([min, max])\n    Common fields for output rows (pass via `fields`):\n      material_id, formula_pretty (or formula), energy_above_hull, formation_energy_per_atom (or formation_energy),\n      band_gap, crystal_system, spacegroup_number, spacegroup_symbol, nsites (or num_sites), density, volume.\n    \n\nmp_download_structure : Download one or more structures from Materials Project into the workspace.\n\nbash_exec : \n    Execute a multi-line bash script inside the workspace (default) and return stdout/stderr.\n    Network access is disabled by default using Linux network namespaces (unshare).\n    Symbolic link operations are disabled; use copy/move operations instead.\n    Stdout/stderr are returned up to max_output_chars per stream.\n    Full streams are persisted to internal metadata audit logs (not for task planning/reading).\n    Keep output short in scripts and print one-line summaries when possible.\n    \n\nwrite_note : Attach a short note to the agent's observation log.\n\nmemory_apply_aider_edits : Apply Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks to memory files.\n","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.2:online","reasoning_effort":"high","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash_exec","description":"Execute a multi-line bash script inside the workspace (default) and return stdout/stderr.\n    Network access is disabled by default using Linux network namespaces (unshare).\n    Symbolic link operations are disabled; use copy/move operations instead.\n    Stdout/stderr are returned up to max_output_chars per stream.\n    Full streams are persisted to internal metadata audit logs (not for task planning/reading).\n    Keep output short in scripts and print one-line summaries when possible.","parameters":{"properties":{"script":{"description":"Bash script to execute (multi-line).","type":"string"},"cwd":{"default":".","description":"Working directory inside project files root.","type":"string"},"timeout_s":{"default":86400.0,"description":"Timeout seconds.","minimum":0.1,"type":"number"},"max_output_chars":{"default":3000,"description":"Max chars returned for stdout/stderr each.","minimum":1000,"type":"integer"},"strict":{"default":true,"description":"Prepend 'set -euo pipefail' for safer scripting.","type":"boolean"},"no_network":{"default":true,"description":"Disable network using unshare network namespace.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["script"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"director_decide","description":"Return the director decision for next action using compact, high-signal fields.","parameters":{"properties":{"state":{"description":"Decision state for the next action.","enum":["PerformNextTask","MinorReviseProposal","MajorReviseProposal","StopAndSynthesize"],"type":"string"},"rationale":{"description":"Very brief decision rationale (usually 1-2 sentences).","type":"string"},"task_packet":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Structured packet for a worker task.","properties":{"goal":{"description":"Concrete worker goal in one short sentence.","title":"Goal","type":"string"},"task_detail":{"description":"Concise execution checklist: non-negotiable constraints, key parameters, and minimal done checks.","title":"Task Detail","type":"string"},"expected_outputs":{"description":"Only concrete deliverables needed for next-step decision.","items":{"type":"string"},"title":"Expected Outputs","type":"array"},"suggested_tools":{"description":"Optional concise tool-name hints for worker; advisory only.","items":{"type":"string"},"title":"Suggested Tools","type":"array"},"reference_hint":{"description":"Short high-value discovery hints (memory files, rg keywords, done-check points); avoid exhaustive lists.","items":{"type":"string"},"title":"Reference Hint","type":"array"}},"required":["goal","task_detail"],"title":"TaskPacket","type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Structured worker task packet."},"updated_proposal_md":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Updated proposal markdown."},"updated_work_packages":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Updated ordered work packages."},"change_log":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Summary of proposal changes."},"needs_human":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Whether human approval is required."},"questions_for_human":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Questions for human decision."},"stop_reason":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Reason for stopping."},"deliverables":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Expected deliverables when stopping."}},"required":["state","rationale"],"type":"object"}}}],"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
