12:09:10 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"You are an execution controller. Use tool calling to advance the current task.\n\nPriority rules:\n- Use tool calling from all available tools to achieve the goal in the context pack.\n- Check tool names and params carefully.\n- Task detail defines the task invariants and done checks. Execute with the minimal non-destructive procedure that satisfies those invariants.\n- Do NOT weaken/skip explicit parameter values in task detail. If task detail conflicts with observed facts, do minimal evidence checks then call `task_fail` with the conflict and evidence.\n- Treat scientific/computational invariants (method + key parameters + convergence criteria) as the highest-priority constraints.\n- Tool schemas are authoritative for argument shapes/defaults; do not re-invent parameter templates in bash scripts.\n- MEMORY policy is system-level: do not edit `MEMORY/**` directly and do not call `memory_apply_aider_edits`.\n\nExecution rules:\n- Do not rerun the same preparation tool with identical parameters if the previous call already succeeded and required artifacts still exist. Prefer reusing and validating existing outputs.\n- Do not trigger expensive reruns purely for path/layout normalization when numerical/physical requirements are already satisfied.\n- Minimize fragmented shell probing: batch related checks into one command/script call instead of many tiny `bash_exec` calls.\n- For routine checks, keep bash output small: prefer focused queries (`rg -n`, `head`, `tail`) and set `max_output_chars` conservatively unless deep debugging is required.\n- Progressive disclosure is mandatory: memory_index_excerpt is short; locate details with `rg`, then read small windows (no large file dumps).\n- Internal metadata audit logs are not task inputs; do not read or reference them in task reasoning.\n- By default, do not generate long markdown reports via `cat <<'MD'`.\n- If a written note is useful, write a short summary under `notes/**` and keep it concise.\n\nParsing policy:\n- Debug triage should prioritize focused, minimal evidence extraction and concise failure signatures.\n- For extracting final numerical results across many calculations (for comparison/reporting), do not manually stitch results with repeated grep commands; run scripts (or parser libraries) to extract in one pass.\n- Prefer mature third-party libraries for parsing and post-analysis when available; avoid reimplementing standard parsers/analysis logic from scratch.\n- Common Python packages are available and preferred when relevant: ase, pymatgen, numpy, matplotlib, scipy, pandas, fitz, requests.\n- Use inline heredoc (`python - <<'PY' ... PY`) for quick result analysis or file inspection that does not need persistence.\n- For actual workload execution (batch processing, long runs, or outputs to be reused/audited), always write script files and execute from disk.\n\nTermination and handoff:\n- Finish with exactly one control call:\n  - `task_finish` when done, with structured fields (summary/facts/files/constraints/open_questions/decisions/next_steps/artifacts).\n  - `task_fail` when blocked by true consistent unexpected errors or fact inconsistencies.\n  - `task_fail` corresponds to `status=blocked` in downstream result mapping.\n  - `task_finish` / `task_fail` must be called alone in its own turn after reviewing tool outputs.\n  - When calling `task_finish`, include in files only the primary script(s) written/executed (kind=script), primary outputs (kind=output/report), and only necessary user-facing logs under project files paths (kind=log).\n- For remote/batch job failures, do one minimal triage (failing status file, stdout/stderr snippets, key inputs) and attempt one focused fix.\n- Do not do open-ended exploration for remote failures (no SSH). If failure persists, call `task_fail` with failed paths, evidence pointers, likely cause, and a minimal rerun/repair plan that reruns only the failed subset.\n- Core output hygiene:\n  - Do NOT paste raw tables, long snippets, logs, or scripts into task_finish.summary.\n  - Put long content into notes/** or reports/** and cite paths in summary/facts/files.\n  - Keep summary concise: short decision/result statements + file pointers.\n  - Do not duplicate the same detail across summary/facts/decisions; keep one canonical mention plus file path.\n  - Result Handoff discipline:\n  - Provide concise, reusable facts with units/conditions/evidence paths for downstream use; avoid low-density narration.\n  - Prefer scientific invariants over run transcripts: keep only durable system/method/result facts.\n  - In `task_finish.facts`, include only high-value results; do not restate process logs or command traces.\n  - In task_finish.open_questions, include only unresolved blockers that can affect the next task; avoid speculative/self-referential questions.\n  - Invariant curation/structuring into MEMORY is handled by the memory patcher.\n- Function tools must be invoked via tool calls. Do NOT put function tool names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n\n\nTermination contract:\n- End with exactly one control tool call in its own turn:\n  - `task_finish` when task is complete.\n  - `task_fail` when blocked by consistent unexpected errors or fact conflicts.\n- Do not output plain final text as the terminal response.","role":"system"},{"content":"<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nRun VASP for isolated triplet O2 in a box (relax + optional static) and report final energy/atom and relaxed O–O bond distance.\n\nTask detail:\n- Execute a VASP ionic relaxation starting from `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/` (single-folder mode). Keep the existing gas-phase settings unchanged (Gamma-only KPOINTS; large ~21 Å cubic cell; `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM=1 1`, `ISYM=0`).\n- Validate the relaxation completed successfully: produce `OUTCAR`, `OSZICAR`, and final `CONTCAR` and show evidence of electronic + ionic convergence (or clearly flag non-convergence and why).\n- If relaxation succeeds, prepare and run a clean static single-point using the relaxed geometry (preferred for final energy): `vasp_sp_prepare` on the relaxation `CONTCAR` with `NSW=0`, `IBRION=-1`, and preserve the same spin settings (`ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM=1 1`).\n- Post-process outputs (static if available, else relax) to extract final `TOTEN` (eV), compute energy per atom `TOTEN/2` (eV/atom), and compute the O–O bond distance from the final relaxed geometry (Å). Write a machine-readable summary artifact (JSON) including file paths used and key INCAR spin parameters.\n\nExpected outputs:\n- vasp_runs/o2_relax/{OUTCAR,OSZICAR,CONTCAR} (or equivalent VASP output folder)\n- (if run) vasp_runs/o2_static/{OUTCAR,OSZICAR,POSCAR,INCAR,KPOINTS,POTCAR}\n- results/o2_summary.json\n- Final TOTEN (eV) and energy/atom (eV/atom) recorded in results/o2_summary.json\n- Final O–O bond distance (Å) recorded in results/o2_summary.json\n- Validation verdict PASS/FAIL with evidence (e.g., grep snippets saved in results/o2_checks.txt or referenced output file paths)\n\nSuggested tools:\nvasp_execute_batch, vasp_sp_prepare, bash_exec, write_note, memory_apply_aider_edits\n\nReference hint:\n- Inputs are ready at `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/` (root contains POSCAR/INCAR/KPOINTS/POTCAR).\n- Spin invariants to preserve: INCAR must include `ISPIN = 2`, `NUPDOWN = 2`, `MAGMOM = 1 1`.\n- Relaxed geometry should be taken from relaxation `CONTCAR` for bond length calculation; final energy should prefer the static single-point `TOTEN` if that run finishes cleanly.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/Test/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Execute VASP relaxation for isolated triplet O2 and report final energy per atom and relaxed O–O bond distance.\n- Current milestone: `task_01` (run_20260227_040233_2ce157) completed O2 structure generation and VASP relaxation input preparation.\n- Latest run artifact: `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/{POSCAR,INCAR,KPOINTS,POTCAR}` plus structure files under `structures/o2/`.\n- Next action: Run VASP relaxation from `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/`, verify convergence, then post-process TOTEN-derived metrics.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. Preserve triplet-spin setup for O2 relaxation (`ISPIN = 2`, `NUPDOWN = 2`, `MAGMOM = 1 1`).\n2. Keep isolated gas-phase setup comparable (large cubic box; Gamma-only `1 1 1` k-point sampling).\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"high","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_molecule_from_smiles","description":"Build a 3D molecule from a SMILES string using RDKit. Specially, pay attention to the formal charge of the SMILES string, RDkit will check the charge and add Hs to the molecule to make it neutral.","parameters":{"properties":{"smiles":{"description":"SMILES string for the molecule.","type":"string"},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional base name for output files; defaults to formula."},"output_path":{"default":"mol","description":"Workspace-relative path prefix; files will be <prefix>.xyz and/or <prefix>.vasp.","type":"string"},"box_padding":{"default":10.0,"description":"Padding (Å) added around the molecule to make a cubic box for POSCAR. Box lattice is around twice the padding value (10A Padding -> 20A Box).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar (with PBC box), xyz (no PBC), or both.","pattern":"^(poscar|xyz|both)$","type":"string"}},"required":["smiles"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_relax_batch","description":"Submit multiple MACE relaxations in one DPDispatcher submission. Preferred tool for batch MACE relaxations.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Root directory containing structure files with lattice (POSCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory to store batch outputs. Results mirror the input directory structure; each input file expands to a folder without suffix (e.g. input_dir/a/c.vasp -> output_root/a/c/opt.vasp). Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"fmax":{"default":0.02,"description":"Force threshold for relaxation in eV/Angstrom.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"maxsteps":{"default":500,"description":"Max steps for relaxation.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name. Recommended options: 'mh-1' (slower, higher accuracy) or 'medium-mpa-0' (faster, lower accuracy).","type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models (e.g. 'omat_pbe'). Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction in mace_mp. Default: false.","type":"boolean"},"relax_lattice":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax lattice/cell together with atomic positions via ASE FrechetCellFilter.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mace_sp_batch","description":"Run MACE single-point jobs for structures under one directory.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory containing structures (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF/VASP).","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Output root for batch results. Must be outside input_dir.","type":"string"},"model":{"default":"mh-1","description":"MACE model name (e.g., mh-1, medium-mpa-0).","type":"string"},"head":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"omat_pbe","description":"Model head for multi-head models. Use empty string to disable."},"dispersion":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dispersion correction.","type":"boolean"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval in seconds when waiting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_root"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_relax_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP relax inputs with calc_type presets and k_product k-mesh.\n    Also can be modified for other calculation types by overriding INCAR via the user_incar_settings.\n    Support exts: .vasp, .cif\n\n    Baseline DFT settings follow Materials Project MPRelaxSet (key defaults):\n    - PBE54 POTCARS, ENCUT=520 eV, PREC=Accurate, ISPIN=2, IBRION=2, LREAL=AUTO, LASPH=True, LWAVE=False, LCHARG=False.\n    - Additional overrides applied based on calc_type: ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.1 for bulk/slab; ISMEAR=0, SIGMA=0.01 for gas.\n    - ISIF policy: bulk with relax_cell=False -> ISIF=2; bulk with relax_cell=True -> ISIF=3.\n      slab and gas always use ISIF=2, where slab forces KPOINTS z=1 and gas forces KPOINTS 1x1x1 with ISYM=0, LREAL=False.\n    - Improved convergence settings: EDIFF=1e-6; NSW=500; EDIFFG=-0.02;\n    - LORBIT is controlled by compute_dos (default False -> LORBIT=0, True -> LORBIT=11).\n    - KPOINTS is generated by k*a=k_product, where a is the lattice constant in Angstrom. Set to 30 by default and sufficient for most systems.\n    - DFT-D3 and DFT+U are disabled by default. Enable them if the system is adsorption system(DFT-D3) or transition metal oxide system(DFT+U).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Path to a structure file with lattice information (POSCAR/CIF) or a directory containing multiple structures. Support exts: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per input structure). If input_path is a file: output_root/<stem>/...; if input_path is a directory, preserve relative subfolders: output_root/<relpath>/<stem>/...","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation type: 'gas'|'bulk'|'slab'. This provides preset INCAR overrides for different calculation types. gas is suitable for small molecules; slab is suitable for surface slab models; bulk is suitable for bulk relaxations. Use relax_cell=true for bulk cell+lattice relaxation (ISIF=3), or keep relax_cell=false for ion-position-only relaxation (ISIF=2).","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"relax_cell":{"default":false,"description":"Whether to relax cell shape/volume (ISIF=3). Only valid when calc_type='bulk'.","type":"boolean"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"Target k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1, forced odd (Gamma-centered); gas always 1x1x1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 Correction (IVDW=11). Enable it for adsorption calculations.","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U relevant settings according to materials project standard. Enable it for Transition Metal Oxide systems.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0) to reduce disk usage.","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass of cell in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"User INCAR overrides as a dict, e.g. {\"MAGMOM\":{\"O\":1},\"NUPDOWN\":2}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null value to remove a key from INCAR. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root","user_incar_settings"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_sp_prepare","description":"Prepare MPRelaxSet-based VASP single-point inputs for structures under a file or directory.","parameters":{"properties":{"input_path":{"description":"Structure file or directory of structures. Supported: .vasp, .cif","type":"string"},"output_root":{"description":"Root directory for generated VASP inputs (one subfolder per structure).","type":"string"},"calc_type":{"default":"bulk","description":"Calculation preset for k-mesh and INCAR defaults.","enum":["gas","bulk","slab"],"type":"string"},"k_product":{"default":30,"description":"k-mesh density via k_i~round(k_product/L_i), min 1.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"use_d3":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT-D3 correction (IVDW=11).","type":"boolean"},"use_dft_plus_u":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DFT+U settings.","type":"boolean"},"compute_dos":{"default":false,"description":"Enable DOS/projection output by setting LORBIT=11. Default false (LORBIT=0).","type":"boolean"},"enable_dipole":{"default":false,"description":"Enable dipole correction helper. When true, default IDIPOL=3 and set DIPOL to the atomic center of mass in fractional coordinates.","type":"boolean"},"user_incar_settings":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Additional INCAR overrides as a dict, e.g. {\"ISMEAR\":0,\"SIGMA\":0.05}. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. Use null value to remove a key from INCAR. calc_type/task-required presets still take precedence on key conflict.","type":"object"}},"required":["input_path","output_root","user_incar_settings"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"build_slab","description":"Build slabs for all terminations of a Miller index from bulk structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of bulk_structure or bulk_dir. When bulk_dir is used, output_root is required.\n    Batch outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path\n    (without suffix) using '__'.","parameters":{"properties":{"bulk_structure":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"bulk_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing bulk structure files for batch slab building."},"miller_index":{"description":"Miller index [h,k,l].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_root":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory to write the slab structures. Required for bulk_dir; defaults to 'slabs' for single file. For bulk_dir, outputs are written under output_root/<slab_id>/..., where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"slab_thickness":{"default":12.0,"description":"Target slab thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"vacuum_thickness":{"default":15.0,"description":"Vacuum thickness (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"supercell":{"default":[1,1,1],"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c] for slab structure after generation.","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"get_symmetry_slab":{"default":false,"description":"If true, returned slabs will ensure top and bottom surfaces are identical. Use it for surface energy calculation.","type":"boolean"},"orthogonal":{"default":false,"description":"If true, convert each slab to an orthogonal c-oriented cell. Useful for grain boundary generation.","type":"boolean"},"lll_reduce":{"default":false,"description":"Apply LLL reduction during slab generation. Not recommended to use unless necessary.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["miller_index"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_layers","description":"Fix (freeze) the bottom N atomic layers of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_layers.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"freeze_layers":{"description":"Number of bottom layers to freeze. Use layer_tol to group layers.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c before applying constraints.","type":"boolean"},"layer_tol":{"default":0.2,"description":"Layer grouping tolerance in Å. 0.2 is suitable for most cases except for highly tilted slabs.","exclusiveMinimum":0.0,"type":"number"}},"required":["freeze_layers"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"fix_atoms_by_height","description":"Fix (freeze) atoms within specified z ranges of slab structure(s).\n\n    Provide exactly one of structure_ref or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<slab_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_fix_atoms_by_height.json.","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file to modify (POSCAR/CIF)."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab structure files to modify."},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path (workspace-relative) for single file."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<slab_id>.vasp where slab_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."},"z_ranges":{"description":"Ranges in Å in Cartesian coordinates; atoms in these z ranges are frozen.","items":{"properties":{"z_min":{"description":"Lower bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"},"z_max":{"description":"Upper bound (Å) in Cartesian coordinates.","type":"number"}},"required":["z_min","z_max"],"type":"object"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"centralize":{"default":false,"description":"Recentre slab along c after applying constraints.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["z_ranges"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"supercell","description":"Create supercells from structure file(s). THIS WILL LOSE ALL SELECTIVE DYNAMICS INFORMATION.\n    Provide exactly one of structure_file or structure_dir. When structure_dir is used, output_dir is required.\n    Batch outputs are written to output_dir/<structure_id>.vasp and a summary JSON is written to\n    output_dir/batch_supercell.json.\n\n    The JSON format is:\n    {\n      \"results\": [\n        {\"input_rel\": \"a/CO.vasp\", \"structure_id\": \"a__CO\", \"output_rel\": \"out/a__CO.vasp\", \"natoms\": 2}\n      ]\n    }","parameters":{"properties":{"structure_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Bulk structure file (POSCAR/CIF/etc.), workspace-relative."},"structure_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing structure files for batch supercell generation."},"supercell":{"description":"Supercell replication [a,b,c].","items":{"type":"integer"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":3,"type":"array"},"output_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output structure path for single structure (workspace-relative, e.g., bulk_supercell.vasp)."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output directory for batch mode. Outputs are written as <output_dir>/<structure_id>.vasp where structure_id encodes the relative input path (without suffix) using '__'."}},"required":["supercell"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"enumerate_adsorption_sites","description":"Enumerate adsorption sites on a slab using ASF. Use it only for small scale placement.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_json:\n    [\n      {\"label\": \"ontop_0\", \"kind\": \"ontop\", \"cart_coords\": [x, y, z]}\n    ]\n    The returned tool data includes the workspace-relative path in \"sites\" and \"sites_json_rel\".","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF), workspace-relative.","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"Which site families to return: all|ontop|bridge|hollow.","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height above surface to sample adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_json":{"default":"adsorption/sites.json","description":"Output JSON path for site list (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"place_adsorbate","description":"Place an adsorbate molecule on a slab. Use it only if for small scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    It writes metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json and an ads_indices index JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF).","type":"string"},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"site":{"default":"auto","description":"Site label like ontop_0|bridge_1|hollow_2 or 'auto' (which use all[0]).","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"output_poscar":{"default":"adsorption/adsorbed.vasp","description":"Output POSCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"}},"required":["slab_file","adsorbate_file"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"generate_batch_adsorption_structures","description":"Generate multiple adsorbed structures up to max_structures. Suitable for large scale placement.\n    This tool keeps selective dynamics of the original slab structure and allows adsorbate to move freely.\n    Input can be a single slab file (slab_file) or a directory of slab files (slab_dir).\n    When slab_dir is used, each slab gets its own subdirectory under output_dir. Max_structures applies per slab.\n    For nested slab_dir layouts, slab_id encodes the relative path (without suffix) using '__'.\n\n    The tool writes a JSON list to output_dir/batch_structures.json and a per-structure\n    metadata sidecar <output>.meta.json with ads_indices.\n    It also writes output_dir/ads_indices.json as an index file:\n    [\n      {\n        \"slab_file_rel\": \"slabs/fe111.vasp\",\n        \"slab_id\": \"fe111\",\n        \"label\": \"ontop_0\",\n        \"output_poscar_rel\": \"adsorption/batch/fe111/ontop_0.vasp\",\n        \"ads_indices_added\": [36],\n        \"ads_indices\": [36]\n      }\n    ]\n    The returned tool data replaces \"structures\" with the workspace-relative path to this JSON file.","parameters":{"properties":{"slab_file":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Slab structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/CIF)."},"slab_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Directory containing slab files for high-throughput placement."},"adsorbate_file":{"description":"Adsorbate molecule file (XYZ).","type":"string"},"mode":{"default":"all","description":"all|ontop|bridge|hollow","type":"string"},"distance":{"default":2.0,"description":"Height used to generate adsorption sites (Å).","minimum":0.0,"type":"number"},"max_structures":{"default":1000,"description":"Maximum number of adsorbed structures to generate.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"adsorption/batch","description":"Directory to write batch POSCARs.","type":"string"}},"required":["adsorbate_file"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_geometry","description":"Generate NEB interpolation geometries in nebmake.pl style.\n\n    The tool validates that initial and final structures have the same element order, atom count,\n    and lattice (within tolerance). Images are written under output_dir/00..(NI+1) with output_filename.\n    Selective dynamics constraints are preserved if present in the input files (ASE handles constraints).","parameters":{"properties":{"initial_path":{"description":"Initial structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"final_path":{"description":"Final structure file (POSCAR/CONTCAR/.vasp/.cif).","type":"string"},"n_images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (NI).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_dir":{"default":"neb_images","description":"Output directory for image folders (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_filename":{"default":"POSCAR","description":"Filename for each image output (e.g., POSCAR).","type":"string"},"interp_mode":{"default":"direct","description":"Output coordinate style when writing POSCAR: direct (fractional) or cartesian.","pattern":"^(direct|cartesian)$","type":"string"},"interp_method":{"default":"linear","description":"Interpolation method: linear or idpp.","pattern":"^(linear|idpp)$","type":"string"},"vtst_wrap":{"default":true,"description":"If true, wrap fractional coordinates into [0,1) before interpolation (VTST nebmake.pl behavior).","type":"boolean"},"overwrite":{"default":false,"description":"If true, overwrite output_dir if it exists.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["initial_path","final_path","n_images"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"make_neb_incar","description":"Generate a VTST NEB/CI-NEB INCAR based on a template INCAR.\n\n    The tool parses the template INCAR (ignores comments/blank lines, case-insensitive keys),\n    applies NEB overrides, and writes the final INCAR along with a patch JSON.","parameters":{"properties":{"template_incar_path":{"description":"Template INCAR path (workspace-relative).","type":"string"},"output_incar_path":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Output INCAR path. If omitted, uses output_dir/INCAR."},"output_dir":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"neb_inputs","description":"Output directory for INCAR and patch JSON (workspace-relative)."},"images":{"description":"Number of intermediate images (IMAGES).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"climb":{"default":false,"description":"Enable CI-NEB with LCLIMB=.TRUE. if true.","type":"boolean"},"iopt":{"default":7,"description":"IOPT value for VTST optimizer (allowed: 7/2/1).","type":"integer"},"ediff":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFF if provided."},"ediffg":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override EDIFFG if provided."},"spring":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Override SPRING if provided."},"potim":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":0.0,"description":"Override POTIM (default 0)."},"additional_overrides":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Additional INCAR overrides as a dict; highest priority and can override required defaults. In this tool, due to pymatgen constraints, MAGMOM/LDAUU/LDAUJ must be provided as symbol:value maps. If not provided, no user override is applied and this tool's default INCAR strategy is used. Use null value to remove a key from INCAR.","type":"object"}},"required":["template_incar_path","images","additional_overrides"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"vasp_execute_batch","description":"Submit VASP runs in one DPDispatcher submission (single-folder or recursive batch modes).","parameters":{"properties":{"input_dir":{"description":"Input directory for VASP execution. Two modes are supported: (1) single-folder mode: input_dir itself is a VASP calc folder containing INCAR and POTCAR; (2) batch mode: recursively discover subfolders containing INCAR and POTCAR. Nested mode is forbidden when input_dir itself is a calc folder and descendants also contain calc folders.","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"description":"Root directory to store outputs. In single-folder mode, results go to output_dir/<basename(input_dir)>. In batch mode, results mirror discovered subfolder layout under output_dir. Must not be inside input_dir. Staging directories under output_dir are cleaned after completion.","type":"string"},"check_interval":{"default":30,"description":"Polling interval seconds","type":"integer"}},"required":["input_dir","output_dir"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_search_materials","description":"Search Materials Project with flexible criteria and write results to CSV.\n\n    Common criteria keys (pass via `criteria`):\n      - material_ids (list[str] or str)\n      - elements (list[str] or str)\n      - chemsys (str)\n      - formula (str)\n      - is_stable (bool)\n      - energy_above_hull ([min, max])\n      - formation_energy ([min, max])\n      - band_gap ([min, max])\n      - crystal_system (str)\n      - spacegroup_number / spacegroup_symbol\n      - num_sites ([min, max])\n      - density ([min, max])\n      - volume ([min, max])\n      - num_elements ([min, max])\n    Common fields for output rows (pass via `fields`):\n      material_id, formula_pretty (or formula), energy_above_hull, formation_energy_per_atom (or formation_energy),\n      band_gap, crystal_system, spacegroup_number, spacegroup_symbol, nsites (or num_sites), density, volume.","parameters":{"properties":{"criteria":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Direct summary.search filters as a dict (keys listed above). Range values may be [min, max].","type":"object"},"fields":{"description":"Fields to include in CSV rows; supports common aliases.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"limit":{"default":50,"description":"Maximum number of hits to return (default 50).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"output_csv":{"description":"Workspace-relative CSV path to write search results.","type":"string"}},"required":["criteria","fields","output_csv"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"mp_download_structure","description":"Download one or more structures from Materials Project into the workspace.","parameters":{"properties":{"mp_ids":{"description":"Materials Project IDs, e.g., ['mp-149', 'mp-13'].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"fmt":{"default":"poscar","description":"Output format: poscar|cif|json.","pattern":"^(poscar|cif|json)$","type":"string"},"output_dir":{"default":"retrieval/mp","description":"Workspace-relative directory to save the structure.","type":"string"}},"required":["mp_ids"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash_exec","description":"Execute a multi-line bash script inside the workspace (default) and return stdout/stderr.\n    Network access is disabled by default using Linux network namespaces (unshare).\n    Symbolic link operations are disabled; use copy/move operations instead.\n    Stdout/stderr are returned up to max_output_chars per stream.\n    Full streams are persisted to internal metadata audit logs (not for task planning/reading).\n    Keep output short in scripts and print one-line summaries when possible.","parameters":{"properties":{"script":{"description":"Bash script to execute (multi-line).","type":"string"},"cwd":{"default":".","description":"Working directory inside project files root.","type":"string"},"timeout_s":{"default":86400.0,"description":"Timeout seconds.","minimum":0.1,"type":"number"},"max_output_chars":{"default":3000,"description":"Max chars returned for stdout/stderr each.","minimum":1000,"type":"integer"},"strict":{"default":true,"description":"Prepend 'set -euo pipefail' for safer scripting.","type":"boolean"},"no_network":{"default":true,"description":"Disable network using unshare network namespace.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["script"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_note","description":"Attach a short note to the agent's observation log.","parameters":{"properties":{"note":{"description":"Freeform note to remember.","type":"string"},"tags":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional tags for filtering later."}},"required":["note"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"task_finish","description":"Signal task completion with concise, non-duplicated structured handoff.","parameters":{"properties":{"summary":{"description":"Concise completed-task summary with key file pointers.","type":"string"},"facts":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only high-signal verified facts from this task."},"files":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Workspace-relative file path.","title":"Path","type":"string"},"description":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Short one-line description.","title":"Description"},"kind":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"File kind, e.g. script/output/report/log.","title":"Kind"}},"required":["path"],"title":"TaskFileRecord","type":"object"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only key files generated or used."},"constraints":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only new/changed constraints."},"open_questions":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only unresolved blockers affecting next tasks."},"decisions":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"properties":{"decision":{"description":"Short decision statement.","title":"Decision","type":"string"},"rationale":{"description":"Brief rationale (one short sentence preferred).","title":"Rationale","type":"string"}},"required":["decision","rationale"],"title":"TaskDecisionRecord","type":"object"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only key decisions with short rationale."},"next_steps":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only immediate suggested next steps."},"artifacts":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Relevant supporting artifact paths when needed."}},"required":["summary"],"type":"object"}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"task_fail","description":"Signal that the current task failed and needs intervention.","parameters":{"properties":{"error":{"description":"A detailed summary of why the task failed.","type":"string"},"needs_human":{"default":true,"description":"Whether a human must intervene.","type":"boolean"},"hint":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional hint for recovery."},"partial_result":{"anyOf":[{"properties":{"summary":{"description":"Concise task outcome summary with key file pointers.","title":"Summary","type":"string"},"facts":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only high-signal verified facts from this task.","title":"Facts"},"files":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"Workspace-relative file path.","title":"Path","type":"string"},"description":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Short one-line description.","title":"Description"},"kind":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"File kind, e.g. script/output/report/log.","title":"Kind"}},"required":["path"],"title":"TaskFileRecord","type":"object"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only key reproducibility/user-facing files.","title":"Files"},"constraints":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only new/changed constraints.","title":"Constraints"},"open_questions":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only unresolved blockers affecting next steps.","title":"Open Questions"},"decisions":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"properties":{"decision":{"description":"Short decision statement.","title":"Decision","type":"string"},"rationale":{"description":"Brief rationale (one short sentence preferred).","title":"Rationale","type":"string"}},"required":["decision","rationale"],"title":"TaskDecisionRecord","type":"object"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only decisions materially affecting downstream work.","title":"Decisions"},"next_steps":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Only immediate actionable next steps.","title":"Next Steps"},"artifacts":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Supporting artifact paths when needed.","title":"Artifacts"}},"required":["summary"],"title":"TaskResultPayload","type":"object"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Optional partial structured result already obtained before failure."}},"required":["error"],"type":"object"}}}],"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
